# The Rust library is not built with -Zsanitizer=thread, so TSan cannot see
# the core's parking_lot mutex or any of its atomics. Image pixels are the one
# buffer the reader thread writes and the host reads: an Image is built whole
# and then published under the core lock (crates/scull-ffi/src/frame.rs), so
# these reads are ordered. Only the reads of that buffer are suppressed; the
# rest of the C side stays checked.
race:touch_image
